WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.643 --> 00:00:04.189
- What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:04.189 --> 00:00:05.819
It's time for another update

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:09.902
on the path to one million
subscriber challenge that I'm on.

00:00:09.902 --> 00:00:11.756
Basically I'm highlighting my journey

00:00:11.756 --> 00:00:13.366
to get to one million subscribers,

00:00:13.366 --> 00:00:15.849
and giving you some tips,
advice, and feedback,

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.326
along the way to help you

00:00:17.326 --> 00:00:19.134
achieve whatever your YouTube goals are.

00:00:19.134 --> 00:00:21.668
Last month when I did the video,

00:00:21.668 --> 00:00:23.835
I had 639,000 subscribers.

00:00:25.313 --> 00:00:27.230
I'm sitting now at 698.

00:00:28.102 --> 00:00:29.185
30,000 swing?

00:00:30.602 --> 00:00:32.300
No, 60,000 swing.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.330
60,000 swing in a positive direction.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:35.324
That's awesome.

00:00:35.324 --> 00:00:37.144
Getting closer to hitting my million goal.

00:00:37.144 --> 00:00:39.288
The past couple videos I've talked about

00:00:39.288 --> 00:00:40.885
the importance of upload frequency.

00:00:40.885 --> 00:00:42.662
I've talked about looking up people

00:00:42.662 --> 00:00:44.392
like Eric Thomas and Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:00:44.392 --> 00:00:46.347
People who are considered
to have immense talent.

00:00:46.347 --> 00:00:47.875
People whose channels I love,

00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:49.809
and they produce some amazing content,

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:52.407
and Eric wasn't producing enough content

00:00:52.407 --> 00:00:54.922
to hit massive YouTube goals.

00:00:54.922 --> 00:00:58.064
Gary now started to increase his frequency

00:00:58.064 --> 00:01:00.061
and is going to pass me soon,

00:01:00.061 --> 00:01:02.503
and so again this may
not be the only thing.

00:01:02.503 --> 00:01:03.972
YouTube is not the only thing.

00:01:03.972 --> 00:01:05.803
I understand these people
have other businesses

00:01:05.803 --> 00:01:07.482
and it's great, I do too.

00:01:07.482 --> 00:01:09.775
This series is focused only on

00:01:09.775 --> 00:01:11.840
how to get subscribers for your channel.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.764
We've talked a lot about upload frequency.

00:01:13.764 --> 00:01:15.523
It's really important for YouTube.

00:01:15.523 --> 00:01:16.895
It's part of their algorithm.

00:01:16.895 --> 00:01:18.479
They want you to upload regularly.

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:20.640
Once a day is the new minimum.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.028
I'm at three per day using my team.

00:01:23.028 --> 00:01:24.910
There's a big growth that you'll get

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.075
from going once per week to once per day.

00:01:27.075 --> 00:01:29.205
Another big jump from once
per day to two per day,

00:01:29.205 --> 00:01:31.652
in terms of how much YouTube
will promote your stuff.

00:01:31.652 --> 00:01:34.062
Between two and three, not as big a gap.

00:01:34.062 --> 00:01:36.378
So it may not be worth
going to that extreme,

00:01:36.378 --> 00:01:38.580
but I'm testing it out and
playing around with it.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:39.413
I encourage you,

00:01:39.413 --> 00:01:41.796
increase your upload
frequency, maintain quality,

00:01:41.796 --> 00:01:44.870
and you'll see a dramatic
rise in your YouTube channel.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.321
It doesn't mean that
you can't have success

00:01:47.321 --> 00:01:49.117
uploading fewer videos,

00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:51.315
but why drive on the side roads

00:01:51.315 --> 00:01:53.163
when you can go on the highway?

00:01:53.163 --> 00:01:54.945
I'm playing the YouTube's algorithm

00:01:54.945 --> 00:01:56.593
and if you do it as well you'll be able

00:01:56.593 --> 00:01:58.425
to beat people who have more skills,

00:01:58.425 --> 00:02:00.541
who have more money, who have
more of a background in it,

00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:02.603
because you understand
the algorithm better.

00:02:02.603 --> 00:02:04.936
Today I want to focus on understanding

00:02:04.936 --> 00:02:08.160
which series are working and which aren't,

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.593
and I'm going to model and
compare another YouTuber,

00:02:10.593 --> 00:02:12.581
that we've had some fun with.

00:02:12.581 --> 00:02:14.334
Grant Cardone, friend of a channel.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.644
He's been on my channel
talking about his book.

00:02:16.644 --> 00:02:18.098
We've done some videos on him.

00:02:18.098 --> 00:02:20.181
A great guy to look at
if you're looking for

00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:23.002
anything about entrepreneurship,
sales, motivation.

00:02:23.002 --> 00:02:24.708
He's a good YouTuber to check out,

00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:26.630
and so I'm going to
compare my channel to his,

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:28.267
and give his some recommendations

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:30.186
to increase his YouTube goals as well.

00:02:30.186 --> 00:02:31.878
Let's pull up the data quickly.

00:02:31.878 --> 00:02:35.286
You can see here I'm at 697,000 subs.

00:02:35.286 --> 00:02:37.094
Grant's at 248.

00:02:37.094 --> 00:02:38.938
What's interesting as we scroll down

00:02:38.938 --> 00:02:40.824
you see that Grant's subs have been

00:02:40.824 --> 00:02:44.089
pretty much consistent
around the 200 range per day

00:02:44.089 --> 00:02:46.090
until recently where it really shot up,

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.162
and he's actually coming close to me,

00:02:48.162 --> 00:02:50.061
and beating me on some days here.

00:02:50.061 --> 00:02:51.364
Good job, Grant,

00:02:51.364 --> 00:02:52.784
and one of the things I want to look at

00:02:52.784 --> 00:02:54.192
dissecting his channel is,

00:02:54.192 --> 00:02:57.757
are all the videos that he's
doing adding to the channel?

00:02:57.757 --> 00:02:59.526
Helping him out with his growth?

00:02:59.526 --> 00:03:00.915
Before jumping in on his,

00:03:00.915 --> 00:03:02.381
I want to show you an example from mine.

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:04.306
The two things that I
really pay attention to

00:03:04.306 --> 00:03:06.556
when I'm evaluating a
new series is watch time,

00:03:06.556 --> 00:03:08.063
because watch time is the single

00:03:08.063 --> 00:03:09.908
most important variable
that YouTube looks at.

00:03:09.908 --> 00:03:12.552
If you are giving YouTube
watch time for their videos,

00:03:12.552 --> 00:03:14.982
they will reward your
videos and rank you higher.

00:03:14.982 --> 00:03:16.692
Every new series that I launch,

00:03:16.692 --> 00:03:17.935
I look at the watch time,

00:03:17.935 --> 00:03:19.522
and then I look at is it leading

00:03:19.522 --> 00:03:21.243
to subscriber growth or not for me?

00:03:21.243 --> 00:03:23.340
If my goal is to get to
a million subscribers,

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.811
that's the name of this series,

00:03:24.811 --> 00:03:26.489
that's the next goal on my list,

00:03:26.489 --> 00:03:27.969
then I need to make sure that

00:03:27.969 --> 00:03:29.546
every series that I launch

00:03:29.546 --> 00:03:31.479
leads to subscriber growth.

00:03:31.479 --> 00:03:35.202
I'll usually give a series
three to four chances to see.

00:03:35.202 --> 00:03:37.275
If it's helping me with
my subscriber growth,

00:03:37.275 --> 00:03:38.314
then I keep it.

00:03:38.314 --> 00:03:39.839
If it's not, I'll kill it,

00:03:39.839 --> 00:03:41.452
unless it serves another purpose.

00:03:41.452 --> 00:03:42.800
If I'm making a sales video.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.328
If I'm showing my life.

00:03:44.328 --> 00:03:46.511
If there's a strategic
reason behind a video,

00:03:46.511 --> 00:03:48.357
besides subscriber growth then I keep it,

00:03:48.357 --> 00:03:49.532
but if there isn't,

00:03:49.532 --> 00:03:51.681
if I'm hoping to use this video
to help me grow my channel

00:03:51.681 --> 00:03:53.370
and it doesn't lead to subscriber growth,

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:54.554
that's when we kill it.

00:03:54.554 --> 00:03:56.554
Let's take a quick look at
two of the videos I did,

00:03:56.554 --> 00:03:58.309
and then we'll jump into Grant's channel.

00:03:58.309 --> 00:04:00.514
This is the first video
that I did on this series.

00:04:00.514 --> 00:04:02.307
How to Get 1 Million YouTube Subscribers.

00:04:02.307 --> 00:04:04.559
This video had 10 days watch time,

00:04:04.559 --> 00:04:05.784
which isn't that great,

00:04:05.784 --> 00:04:07.734
and only led to eight subscriptions.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:10.144
That's not a fantastic start

00:04:10.144 --> 00:04:12.275
for what a video would get on my channel,

00:04:12.275 --> 00:04:14.476
but it's worth an extra
shot, an extra test.

00:04:14.476 --> 00:04:16.749
The second one I did was
me and Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:04:16.749 --> 00:04:18.394
That was the last one of the series.

00:04:18.394 --> 00:04:20.230
This one had 40 days watch time,

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:24.461
and it drove 62 new
subscribers, which is better.

00:04:24.461 --> 00:04:27.620
This is version three
right now in the series.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.856
This one right here is version three

00:04:29.856 --> 00:04:31.348
and we'll see how well it does.

00:04:31.348 --> 00:04:33.669
This will help tell me am I
going to keep this series or not?

00:04:33.669 --> 00:04:35.411
I highly encourage you to look at

00:04:35.411 --> 00:04:37.841
for every video series that you launch,

00:04:37.841 --> 00:04:40.055
whatever new ideas that you have,

00:04:40.055 --> 00:04:42.115
give it three or four tests
to get some good data on,

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.737
and does it lead to watch time,

00:04:43.737 --> 00:04:45.623
and does it lead to
subscribers for your channel?

00:04:45.623 --> 00:04:46.654
If it does, keep it.

00:04:46.654 --> 00:04:47.829
If it doesn't, kill it.

00:04:47.829 --> 00:04:49.591
Let's jump in on Grant's channel,

00:04:49.591 --> 00:04:51.936
and I can show you what he's doing.

00:04:51.936 --> 00:04:53.190
This is Grant's channel,

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:56.804
and Grant is doing an
amazing job at the content.

00:04:56.804 --> 00:04:58.301
It's really rare to find people

00:04:58.301 --> 00:05:00.317
who are keeping up with me on the content.

00:05:00.317 --> 00:05:02.101
I think actually recently
he's ahead of me.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.358
This is two hours ago.

00:05:03.358 --> 00:05:06.747
17 hours, 18 hours, 18
hours, 19 hours, 22 hours.

00:05:06.747 --> 00:05:08.067
One thing I would say,

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:09.546
if you're going to post this much,

00:05:09.546 --> 00:05:11.288
spread it out a little bit more.

00:05:11.288 --> 00:05:13.761
If you're going to post
five, six videos in a day,

00:05:13.761 --> 00:05:16.172
spread them out over a
couple hours each time,

00:05:16.172 --> 00:05:17.540
so they're not back to back

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.330
because it gives a little more room

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.172
for the videos to breathe.

00:05:21.172 --> 00:05:22.728
Here 22, 19, 18, 18, 17.

00:05:22.728 --> 00:05:25.048
These are all going to be lumped together,

00:05:25.048 --> 00:05:27.205
and all of these videos
could have had more views

00:05:27.205 --> 00:05:28.405
if you spaced them out.

00:05:28.405 --> 00:05:29.752
Like this one that was two hours ago,

00:05:29.752 --> 00:05:31.338
one day, two day, and so on.

00:05:31.338 --> 00:05:33.856
It's great to see Grant
uploading tons of content

00:05:33.856 --> 00:05:36.359
and I consider Grant to
be an amazing speaker,

00:05:36.359 --> 00:05:38.839
and has lots of great
wisdom and advice to share.

00:05:38.839 --> 00:05:39.812
What's the deal?

00:05:39.812 --> 00:05:41.490
He's uploading tons of content,

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:43.959
but is stuck at 250,000 subs.

00:05:43.959 --> 00:05:45.878
Let's break down some of the series,

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.929
so we can look at where he's doing right,

00:05:47.929 --> 00:05:50.185
and what he's doing wrong.

00:05:50.185 --> 00:05:52.278
This is a typical Grant video.

00:05:52.278 --> 00:05:54.474
The news ones coming out at least.

00:05:54.474 --> 00:05:55.925
46 days watch time.

00:05:55.925 --> 00:05:56.975
That's awesome.

00:05:56.975 --> 00:05:58.423
18 subscriptions driven.

00:05:58.423 --> 00:05:59.717
Here's another one.

00:05:59.717 --> 00:06:01.291
150 days watch time.

00:06:01.291 --> 00:06:02.982
13 subscriptions driven.

00:06:02.982 --> 00:06:05.242
27 days watch time, 12
subscriptions driven.

00:06:05.242 --> 00:06:07.786
He's driving between 10 to 20 subscribers

00:06:07.786 --> 00:06:09.943
per new video that he puts out.

00:06:09.943 --> 00:06:11.237
That's about Grant.

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.999
This is all Grant just talking,

00:06:12.999 --> 00:06:14.558
ranting into his phone.

00:06:14.558 --> 00:06:16.378
It doesn't have to be a setup.

00:06:16.378 --> 00:06:18.189
He's just going off the cuff,

00:06:18.189 --> 00:06:20.714
and Grant is one of
the best at doing this.

00:06:20.714 --> 00:06:22.507
Going off the cuff, being live,

00:06:22.507 --> 00:06:24.788
sharing his opinions and
rolling with the punches.

00:06:24.788 --> 00:06:27.366
A typical Grant video
where he's just doing that,

00:06:27.366 --> 00:06:29.304
leads to 10 to 20 subs, which is great.

00:06:29.304 --> 00:06:31.236
Next time I'll look at some of his series.

00:06:31.236 --> 00:06:33.391
This is a series that he
has called Ask the Pro.

00:06:33.391 --> 00:06:35.984
Grant is not actually
in these videos here,

00:06:35.984 --> 00:06:38.614
and look at the difference on the videos.

00:06:38.614 --> 00:06:42.703
Five days watch time,
zero subscriptions driven.

00:06:42.703 --> 00:06:44.346
The other really important thing

00:06:44.346 --> 00:06:46.216
to understand about the YouTube algorithm,

00:06:46.216 --> 00:06:48.087
and this is worth a
pause on this point here.

00:06:48.087 --> 00:06:52.363
If you have a video that
underperforms your average,

00:06:52.363 --> 00:06:55.315
if you have a video that does
really poorly on your channel,

00:06:55.315 --> 00:06:57.973
it actually hurts your future video.

00:06:57.973 --> 00:07:00.234
This was an important lesson I learned.

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:02.180
I was just putting up tons of content.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.308
Content after content.

00:07:03.308 --> 00:07:05.384
Figure let YouTube pick
what's going to work.

00:07:05.384 --> 00:07:06.986
It's adding value to the audience.

00:07:06.986 --> 00:07:08.231
I don't care if a video only

00:07:08.231 --> 00:07:09.957
gets 1,000 views or 3,000 views.

00:07:09.957 --> 00:07:11.450
Doesn't really make a difference.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.098
It's just still high quality content.

00:07:13.098 --> 00:07:15.607
If a video does not do well,

00:07:15.607 --> 00:07:18.911
especially considering what
your average video will do,

00:07:18.911 --> 00:07:22.520
then that video hurts the future videos

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.941
that come out on your channel.

00:07:24.941 --> 00:07:27.128
The flip side is, if a
video does really well,

00:07:27.128 --> 00:07:28.305
if it takes off,

00:07:28.305 --> 00:07:29.802
then that video will help your

00:07:29.802 --> 00:07:31.338
future videos on your channel.

00:07:31.338 --> 00:07:33.198
You always want to be producing content

00:07:33.198 --> 00:07:34.649
that is better than the average.

00:07:34.649 --> 00:07:37.838
It keeps raising the bar on
watch time for the channel

00:07:37.838 --> 00:07:39.482
but this is really important,

00:07:39.482 --> 00:07:41.008
because if you have a series

00:07:41.008 --> 00:07:43.176
that is at zero subscribers growth,

00:07:43.176 --> 00:07:46.451
and it's underperforming
compared to your average,

00:07:46.451 --> 00:07:49.005
then whatever future
video that Grant puts out,

00:07:49.005 --> 00:07:50.620
that may be him ranting,

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:52.341
even though those typically overperform,

00:07:52.341 --> 00:07:54.336
YouTube will not rank it as well,

00:07:54.336 --> 00:07:57.590
because this Ask the
Pro video underperforms.

00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:59.960
That's where it's really
really really important

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.489
to pay attention to the series

00:08:01.489 --> 00:08:02.792
that are working or not,

00:08:02.792 --> 00:08:04.148
and the ones that aren't kill them,

00:08:04.148 --> 00:08:05.844
because they hurt all your future videos.

00:08:05.844 --> 00:08:08.035
Let's jump back in and
look at this stream again.

00:08:08.035 --> 00:08:09.329
This is Ask the Pro,

00:08:09.329 --> 00:08:11.334
and maybe it's because
Grant's not in this show,

00:08:11.334 --> 00:08:12.659
that it doesn't do as well.

00:08:12.659 --> 00:08:14.891
This often happens with
personality driven channels

00:08:14.891 --> 00:08:16.951
when it's under somebody's name

00:08:16.951 --> 00:08:18.530
and then somebody comes on

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:19.755
and Grant's not there,

00:08:19.755 --> 00:08:20.966
the video won't do as well.

00:08:20.966 --> 00:08:23.074
This video had zero subscribers growth.

00:08:23.074 --> 00:08:24.900
Here's another one, Ask the Pro.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.948
Same guy, has another guest coming on.

00:08:26.948 --> 00:08:30.761
11 days watch, negative
one subscriptions driven.

00:08:30.761 --> 00:08:34.286
He actually lost subscribers
because of this video.

00:08:34.286 --> 00:08:35.457
He lost a subscriber.

00:08:35.457 --> 00:08:36.704
Instead of it growing,

00:08:36.704 --> 00:08:38.217
he's losing base because of this.

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:40.619
Maybe there are other Ask the Pro videos.

00:08:40.619 --> 00:08:42.587
I haven't gone too far back in the series.

00:08:42.587 --> 00:08:45.283
Maybe I happened to pick
two that underperformed,

00:08:45.283 --> 00:08:47.407
but in general if a video series

00:08:47.407 --> 00:08:49.207
is leading to negative growth,

00:08:49.207 --> 00:08:50.951
and is not doing well compared

00:08:50.951 --> 00:08:53.058
to your usual videos on time watched,

00:08:53.058 --> 00:08:54.736
then it's time to kill that series

00:08:54.736 --> 00:08:56.324
and move on to something else,

00:08:56.324 --> 00:08:58.272
unless it serves a strategic purpose

00:08:58.272 --> 00:09:00.060
to help in your main business.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.256
How you make money, how
you add value, grow.

00:09:03.256 --> 00:09:04.908
Next I want to jump in on

00:09:04.908 --> 00:09:06.396
some of Grant's shorter clips.

00:09:06.396 --> 00:09:08.067
What he'll often do here is,

00:09:08.067 --> 00:09:10.137
you'll have a main big video like this.

00:09:10.137 --> 00:09:13.248
This is one of Grant's
videos, Cardone Zone,

00:09:13.248 --> 00:09:14.936
talking about saving for retirement.

00:09:14.936 --> 00:09:17.064
72 days watched, seven
subscriptions driven.

00:09:17.064 --> 00:09:17.966
It's okay.

00:09:17.966 --> 00:09:20.640
It's actually interesting
how his set pieces like this

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.566
underperform his live stuff,

00:09:22.566 --> 00:09:24.262
because this takes a lot of time.

00:09:24.262 --> 00:09:26.627
There's setup time, there's
crew time, there's questions.

00:09:26.627 --> 00:09:28.213
there's a lot of effort that

00:09:28.213 --> 00:09:29.806
goes into making one of these videos,

00:09:29.806 --> 00:09:32.457
for it to only have seven
subscriptions driven,

00:09:32.457 --> 00:09:34.343
compared to something like this that's 18.

00:09:34.343 --> 00:09:35.176
This is 13.

00:09:35.176 --> 00:09:36.518
This took Grant 10 minutes.

